WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:14.082
Hi! When we tell someone what another person said, English has special rules. This is called reported speech. Today we'll learn how tenses, pronouns and time words change.

2
00:00:14.232 --> 00:00:20.610
Direct speech uses quotation marks and the exact words: Mia said, I am tired today.

3
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:29.322
In reported speech: Mia said that she was tired that day. I becomes she, am becomes was, and today becomes that day.

4
00:00:29.472 --> 00:00:39.018
Rule one: the tense moves one step back into the past. Am and is become was, are becomes were, will becomes would, and can becomes could.

5
00:00:39.168 --> 00:00:50.250
Rule two: time and place words change too. Today becomes that day, tomorrow becomes the next day, here becomes there, and now becomes then.

6
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.938
Rule three: pronouns change. Tom said, I like my new bag.

7
00:00:56.088 --> 00:01:02.370
When we report it, I becomes he and my becomes his: Tom said that he liked his new bag.

8
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:09.930
In a question, ask yourself: who is reporting it now, and who was the speaker talking about?

9
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:17.898
For a yes-no question, use asked if. Put it in statement order, with no question mark: He asked if I was coming.

10
00:01:18.048 --> 00:01:24.618
For a question with where or what, keep that word: She asked where I lived. Not where did I live.

11
00:01:24.768 --> 00:01:33.498
For a command, use told plus a person plus to. Dad told us not to shout. For don't, use not to.

12
00:01:33.648 --> 00:01:37.818
Watch out! She asked me where did I live is wrong!

13
00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:45.114
In reported speech, a question uses statement word order: where I lived. No did, and no question mark.

14
00:01:45.264 --> 00:01:51.858
Remember: once a question is reported, it takes normal sentence order.

15
00:01:52.008 --> 00:02:04.530
Your turn! Ben said, I will call you tomorrow. In reported speech: Ben said that he ___ call me ___. Pause and think.

16
00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:12.522
The answers are would and the next day: Ben said that he would call me the next day. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:12.672 --> 00:02:24.594
Another one! The teacher said, Open your books. It becomes: The teacher told us ___ our books. Pause and think.

18
00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:32.922
The answer is to open. A command uses told, a person, and to. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:33.072 --> 00:02:44.082
Last one! Amy asked, Is it raining? It becomes: Amy asked ___ it was raining. Pause and think.

20
00:02:44.232 --> 00:02:49.410
The answer is if, or whether. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:49.560 --> 00:03:03.138
Remember: in reported speech, the tense steps back, and pronouns, time and place words change. Questions use asked if or the question word, in statement order. Commands use told, a person, and to.

22
00:03:03.288 --> 00:03:08.322
Try reporting something a family member said today!

